Parity unit : page:battery/Energy   kind=page   web route=/energy
Web source  : web/src/features/battery/pages/EnergyPage.tsx
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/EnergyPage/{EnergyPage.Model.cs, EnergyPage.Source.cs,
              EnergyPage.ViewModel.cs, EnergyPage.cs}  (real in-repo convention; see APPROACH)
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feeds), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling
  W7 TrueCostPage / VehicleCostPage / TimelinePage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "Features/Battery/EnergyPage.xaml + EnergyPageViewModel.cs under apps/windows/TeslaSync/" is mapped onto these
  real conventions (no drift hidden — this note is the disclosure). The surface registers itself with the W4
  ShellPageFactory by route name "Energy" (already in RouteTable.cs L104 -> /energy) via ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Battery. Page registered:
  _viewModel.PageFactory.Register("Energy", static () => new FeatureViews.Battery.EnergyPage());
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest's three hooks are ported as three single-responsibility cache-then-network
  ports bound through the ObservableObject view-model (P1/S8), keeping the web hook names at the C# call sites:
    * useEnergyStats            -> IEnergyStatsSource / EnergyStatsClientSource
                                   GET /vehicles/{vehicleID}/energy?days=30 (op get_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_energy)
    * useChargingSessionsPaginated -> IChargingSessionsSource / ChargingSessionsClientSource
                                   GET /charging-sessions?vehicle_id&limit=100&offset=0&start&end (op get_api_v1_charging_sessions)
                                   over the rolling 30-day window (web default range), snake_case params (ADR-004 #8 no camelCase).
    * useChargingTelemetryLatest -> IChargingTelemetryLatestSource / ChargingTelemetryLatestClientSource
                                   GET /charging-telemetry/latest?vehicle_id (op get_api_v1_charging_telemetry_latest)
  The scoped vehicle is resolved from the shared IWidgetVehicleSource (native useSelectedVehicle / vehicles[0]
  fallback); with no vehicle every read short-circuits to RepositoryResult.Empty (web `enabled: vehicleId !== null`).
  No HTTP touches the view. The view-model reads SI from the API and the projection converts ONLY at the display
  boundary (ADR P1/S5: UnitConverters/UnitFormatters/ScalarFormatters); the wire JSON round-trips losslessly
  through the cache (raw JsonElement) and the {data:…} envelope is unwrapped by the tolerant parsers.
- States (ADR-006): the web page renders the skeleton on useEnergyStats.isLoading, the QueryError on statsError,
  and otherwise the full body with PER-SECTION empty states (the empty hero when there is no energy data yet, each
  ChartContainer's empty body, the empty sessions table). The native port reproduces these as visible Fluent
  regions and NEVER hides a section: EnergyState.Loading -> TsStatGridSkeleton(4)+TsStatGridSkeleton(6)+TsTableSkeleton×2;
  EnergyState.Error -> TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent) + Retry; EnergyState.Ready/Stale/Offline -> the nine panels,
  with the hero swapping to a TsEmptyState and every chart container showing its empty body when its source is empty.
  A populated-but-empty stats response stays Ready (web parity) — only a first-load failure with no cache is Error.
- SI units: distance m->km/mi, energy Wh->Wh/kWh, power W->kW, efficiency Wh/m->Wh/km|Wh/mi are all restated at
  projection time via the shared converters; nothing non-SI is stored or computed. Imperial flips the efficiency
  gauge/series unit to Wh/mi and the energy unit to kWh (test Projection_efficiency_unit_switches_to_imperial).
- a11y/dark mode: every panel/chart publishes AutomationProperties names (TsChartContainer.AccessibleSummary carries
  each chart's web ariaLabel); the design-token components (TsGlassPanel/Typography/charts) honor light/dark + high
  contrast via the W1/W2 token dictionaries; the page exposes a Group AutomationPeer.
- i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal flows through ILocalizer.GetString("<web key>", "<web default>") with the
  exact web key names; 43 of the 56 keys were already in the platform catalog (translation.energy.* /
  translation.common.noData), and the 13 keys the web added after the last catalog generation
  (energy.chart.energy, energy.chart.*.aria ×4, energy.cost_decimal.* ×6, energy.table.cost_decimal, energy.empty.hero)
  were appended to Strings/en|ar|he/Resources.resw so all 56 resolve from the catalog (xml re-validated).

